                 ⚠ CORRECTED 2026-09-09. The first version of this NOTICE, and
                 the README paragraph about it, had SAMPLE and POPULATION the
                 wrong way round in every sentence that named a list. The Ada
                 was right throughout: Conflict_Alt counts S-entries missing
                 from Q, matching upstream with S the sample. The prose was
                 wrong. An adversarial review caught it the same night; the
                 correction is kept here rather than quietly made.

                 ⚠ SCOPE, narrower than upstream.
                 · A substitution is one whole-number key. Upstream compares
                   position, reference base and alternate base together; any
                   encoding of the three into one key that keeps distinct
                   substitutions distinct preserves every statement here.
                 · Lists hold at most 8 keys.
                 · The exclusion of missing and deleted coordinates and the
                   optional coordinate filter (lines 41-58) are NOT modelled.
                   The core takes the two lists as already filtered.

                 WHAT THE PROVER REFUSED, kept on the record. The first claim
                 written for Score also said it never exceeds the POPULATION
                 list's length (NQ). GNATprove could not discharge it, and it is
                 false: if the sample list holds one key three times and the
                 population holds it once, support is 3 and the score is 3,
                 above the population's length of 1. Upstream's lists are
                 duplicate-free by construction (one substitution per genome
                 coordinate), so the bound holds there — but this core does not
                 assume distinctness, so it does not claim the bound. It was
                 withdrawn from the claim, not added as an assumption.

                 WHAT IS PROVED, graded. The four inductions carry the weight:
                 membership agrees with the quantified statement; support never
                 exceeds the sample's length; conflict_alt = |S| - support and
                 conflict_ref = |Q| - support(Q against S) — the two partitions,
                 each proved on the recursive function's own postcondition.
                 The rest follows in one step and is labelled so: Score never
                 exceeds support (both conflicts are non-negative), never
                 exceeds the sample's length, never falls below minus the two
                 lengths; and Mutual_Containment_Scores_Full is a corollary of
                 the two partitions under its precondition.

                 Solver grade: all three of Z3, CVC5 and Alt-Ergo alone
                 discharge every check of this package.

